section: base
synopsis: Fix a bug in `threadWaitRead`/`threadWaitWrite` in the MIO I/O
  manager on macOS. The symptom was that if a file descriptor (fd) was closed,
  without using `closeFdWith`, while a thread was still waiting on that fd
  using `threadWaitRead`/`threadWaitWrite`, then subsequent uses of
  `threadWaitRead`/`threadWaitWrite` on unrelated files (that happened to get
  allocated the same fd number) would block forever.
description:
  ``registerFd_`` concluded from the callback table alone that an fd was
  already armed in the polling backend, and so called the backend only when
  the events it wanted differed from the ones the table recorded.  That holds
  only while the two agree, which they stop doing once an fd is closed without
  ``closeFdWith``: the kernel drops the registration, the table keeps it, and
  the number is handed straight back out.  It now always calls the backend.
